      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T14:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An SSE stream is silent by nature, and the only thing keeping the QUIC\nconnection under this default 30s timeout is the server\u0027s \"ping\" heartbeat (EventStreamResponse) - which is configured by \"heartbeat-interval\" and defaults to  10000(0 disables it). With pings off, a healthy but quiet subscription now\nends by itself and the listener just sees onStreamEnd(). Could the yang description mention that dependency between these config values?",
      "revId": "deb858c2ced56845c3a616d8c47f1bda82694eaa",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
